
# .agents Claude/Cursor bridge + graphify output (regenerated locally, never commit)
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/agents/
/.claude/skills/
# Host-authored commands are this project's own source, not bridge output.
# install.sh only ever writes .claude/commands/agents/, so a file at the root of
# commands/ is safe to track. The pattern excludes the directory's *contents*
# rather than the directory itself: git does not descend into an excluded
# directory, so a negation under `/.claude/commands/` would never be consulted.
/.claude/commands/*
!/.claude/commands/wa-export.md
/.claude/settings.local.json
# Same shape as `.claude/commands/` above, and for the same reason: the Cursor
# entry point ADR-0001 declares is this project's own source, not bridge output,
# so the directory's *contents* are excluded and the host-authored file is
# re-included. Excluding the directory itself would make the negation dead.
/.cursor/commands/*
!/.cursor/commands/wa-export.md
/.cursor/rules/
/.cursor/agents/
/.cursor/mcp.json
/graphify-out/
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.Python
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
dist/
build/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.agent_state/
docs/active_state.json

# Customer chat exports (ADR-0001 / ADR-0002) — never commit
/data/

# Ephemeral session telemetry (agents.md §4)
/memory/
